# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Target network for this deployment: 'mainnet' | 'testnet' (default: testnet)
# Drives CKB client, BTC network, rgbpp scripts and wallet network preference.
# In production: set per-deployment and leave the switcher off (see below).
NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK=testnet

# Show the in-app network switcher and honor its choice. Set to 'true' for
# preview/dev environments where you want to flip between mainnet/testnet
# without restarting. Unset (or any other value) in production — production
# should be two separate deployments, each pinned via NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOW_NETWORK_SWITCH=true

# Canonical site origin, used to turn relative metadata URLs (Open Graph /
# Twitter-card images) into absolute ones. Set to the public origin this
# deployment is served from. Unset → code falls back to the netlify preview URL,
# which is correct for preview. In the leapfi.app production deployment, set:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://leapfi.app

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-side only (never exposed to the browser)
#
# The app reads RGB++ data through three independent providers, each behind its
# own proxy route. They are separate because they are becoming separate
# services; see lib/services/providers/types.ts.
#
#   /api/indexer   RGBPP_INDEXER_*   rgbpp-indexer — RGB++ state (cells,
#                                    balances, cross-chain tx status, history)
#   /api/gateway   RGBPP_GATEWAY_*   rgbpp-gateway — Bitcoin access and the
#                                    RGB++ SPV proof. NOT BUILT YET
#   /api/metadata  RGBPP_METADATA_*  asset metadata — symbol, name, decimals,
#                                    DOB cluster. NO OWNER YET
#
# Each provider supports two shapes:
#
#   1. SINGLE-NETWORK (production): set <PREFIX>_URL (+ _TOKEN / _ORIGIN).
#      The network cookie is ignored; the deployment is pinned via
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK.
#
#   2. DUAL-NETWORK (preview/dev with the switcher on): set both
#      <PREFIX>_URL_MAINNET and <PREFIX>_URL_TESTNET, each with its own
#      _TOKEN / _ORIGIN. The proxy routes per request from the switcher cookie.
#      If either dual var is set, the single-network vars are ignored.
#
# _TOKEN and _ORIGIN are optional — set them only for an upstream that requires
# auth. When _TOKEN is set the proxy injects `Authorization: Bearer <token>`,
# and `Origin: <origin>` alongside it.

# ── rgbpp-indexer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://github.com/fghdotio/rgbpp-indexer-opus5high
#
# Required. There is no fallback for this one on purpose: btc-assets-api cannot
# stand in for the indexer — the routes are entirely different — so a missing
# value fails loudly at the proxy rather than 404ing every asset lookup.
RGBPP_INDEXER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# RGBPP_INDEXER_TOKEN=
# RGBPP_INDEXER_ORIGIN=
#
# Dual-network (preview/dev): one indexer instance per network.
# RGBPP_INDEXER_URL_MAINNET=
# RGBPP_INDEXER_URL_TESTNET=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# ── rgbpp-gateway ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Serves /bitcoin/v1/* and /rgbpp/v1/btc-spv/proof.
#
# rgbpp-gateway does not exist yet. Leave these unset and the proxy falls back
# to the legacy RGBPP_API_* vars below — btc-assets-api answers exactly these
# routes, which is what makes it a drop-in stand-in. Point RGBPP_GATEWAY_URL at
# the real gateway when it ships; nothing else has to change.
# RGBPP_GATEWAY_URL=
# RGBPP_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
# RGBPP_GATEWAY_ORIGIN=
# RGBPP_GATEWAY_URL_MAINNET=
# RGBPP_GATEWAY_URL_TESTNET=

# ── asset metadata ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Serves /rgbpp/v1/assets/type.
#
# No owner yet — same fallback to RGBPP_API_* as the gateway. It has its own
# vars so that moving metadata to a different service later is an env change.
# RGBPP_METADATA_URL=
# RGBPP_METADATA_TOKEN=
# RGBPP_METADATA_ORIGIN=
# RGBPP_METADATA_URL_MAINNET=
# RGBPP_METADATA_URL_TESTNET=

# ── btc-assets-api (legacy fallback) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Used only by the gateway and metadata routes, and only while their real
# services are unbuilt. Delete these once both have shipped.
RGBPP_API_URL=https://api-testnet.rgbpp.com
# RGBPP_API_TOKEN=
# RGBPP_API_ORIGIN=https://your-deployed-domain.com
#
# RGBPP_API_URL_MAINNET=https://api.rgbpp.com
# RGBPP_API_TOKEN_MAINNET=
# RGBPP_API_ORIGIN_MAINNET=https://your-deployed-domain.com
# RGBPP_API_URL_TESTNET=https://api-testnet.rgbpp.com
# RGBPP_API_TOKEN_TESTNET=
# RGBPP_API_ORIGIN_TESTNET=
